## Why This Question Is Asked
This evaluates cost modeling for federated, multi-app ML with privacy constraints—a realistic production use case at companies like Google (Gboard), Apple, and Meta. It tests ability to identify cost drivers, trade-offs between privacy and accuracy, and phased rollout planning under regulatory constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning with secure aggregation and differential privacy
- Cross-app governance, regional data locality (GDPR, CCPA, PIPL)
- Bandwidth, energy, and memory budgeting on mobile devices
- Model drift detection, concept drift, and maintenance pipelines
- Phased regional rollout with go/no-go gates

## Code Example
```javascript
function calculateCBAPhase(devices, roundsPerDay, daysPerMonth, payloadKB, costPerGB) {
  const activeDevices = devices * 0.30;
  const monthlyUplinkGB = activeDevices * roundsPerDay * daysPerMonth * payloadKB / 1024 / 1024;
  const monthlyCost = monthlyUplinkGB * costPerGB;
  return {
    devices, activeDevices, monthlyUplinkGB, monthlyCost,
    breakEvenUsers: monthlyCost / 0.10
  };
}

function rolloutPhase(phase, criteria) {
  return {
    phase,
    go: criteria.every(c => c.passed),
    gates: criteria
  };
}
```

